{
  "case_id": "2011-10-6549",
  "document_hash": "238955ce48d17b98acdaf3d5add3f8e92643fc88d03e10fe0a8a67f790cdb686",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-10-6549",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "238955ce48d17b98acdaf3d5add3f8e92643fc88d03e10fe0a8a67f790cdb686",
      "evidence_id": "ev-238955ce48d1-0000-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:06 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Cain",
      "case_id": "2011-10-6549",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "238955ce48d17b98acdaf3d5add3f8e92643fc88d03e10fe0a8a67f790cdb686",
      "evidence_id": "ev-238955ce48d1-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But for a valid exercise of the Attorney General's authority under subsection (d), Mr. Reynolds had no obligation to register under SORNA, could not initially register under SORNA, and, therefore, was not subject to SORNA's criminal penalties."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-10-6549",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "238955ce48d17b98acdaf3d5add3f8e92643fc88d03e10fe0a8a67f790cdb686",
      "evidence_id": "ev-238955ce48d1-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Was the -- is the Wetterling Act retroactive?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-10-6549",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "238955ce48d17b98acdaf3d5add3f8e92643fc88d03e10fe0a8a67f790cdb686",
      "evidence_id": "ev-238955ce48d1-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could you clarify that answer? The -- are you admitting that there were no criminal enforcement options for the Attorney General under the Wetterling Act for acts committed prior to 1996?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Cain",
      "case_id": "2011-10-6549",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "238955ce48d17b98acdaf3d5add3f8e92643fc88d03e10fe0a8a67f790cdb686",
      "evidence_id": "ev-238955ce48d1-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "and then fail to register after you are obligated under SORNA to register is a crime, yes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Cain",
      "case_id": "2011-10-6549",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "238955ce48d17b98acdaf3d5add3f8e92643fc88d03e10fe0a8a67f790cdb686",
      "evidence_id": "ev-238955ce48d1-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We actually don't know the answer to that question, because the Attorney General has not issued regulations instructing offenders what to do."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-10-6549",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "238955ce48d17b98acdaf3d5add3f8e92643fc88d03e10fe0a8a67f790cdb686",
      "evidence_id": "ev-238955ce48d1-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would he have been in compliance with SORNA under the final rules today, the interim rules when they were passed, or on the date that he left if he had when he traveled, or a reasonable time thereafter, told his State of conviction that he had moved?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Cain",
      "case_id": "2011-10-6549",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "238955ce48d17b98acdaf3d5add3f8e92643fc88d03e10fe0a8a67f790cdb686",
      "evidence_id": "ev-238955ce48d1-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We were denied the ability to do that below."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Arbus Sherry",
      "case_id": "2011-10-6549",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "238955ce48d17b98acdaf3d5add3f8e92643fc88d03e10fe0a8a67f790cdb686",
      "evidence_id": "ev-238955ce48d1-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Number one, for offenders like Reynolds that are already registered, there's nothing more to be done as far as registration goes. All they need to do is to keep the information current and to keep it updated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2011-10-6549",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "238955ce48d17b98acdaf3d5add3f8e92643fc88d03e10fe0a8a67f790cdb686",
      "evidence_id": "ev-238955ce48d1-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: And what is a reasonable time?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Cain",
      "case_id": "2011-10-6549",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "238955ce48d17b98acdaf3d5add3f8e92643fc88d03e10fe0a8a67f790cdb686",
      "evidence_id": "ev-238955ce48d1-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They acknowledge the opposite themselves in footnote 12, where they say that -- that a government or a State will have been deemed to substantially implement SORNA if it registers pre-enactment and pre-implementation sex offenders who remain in the system as registrants, as well as other people."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-10-6549",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "238955ce48d17b98acdaf3d5add3f8e92643fc88d03e10fe0a8a67f790cdb686",
      "evidence_id": "ev-238955ce48d1-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Chief Justice Roberts: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
